From 35a95578ad94868044c60e5d898a5e9e60c024c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tylnexttime <tylnexttime@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:19:38 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Marian 0009 prefill source switch: --moe-prefill-source
 mmap|p3, default mmap, 0008's path only with p3

0008 sent the large-batch selective copy (llama_context::sched_copy_experts, ubatches above 32 tokens) through the P3
source whenever --moe-miss-source was ring or tier. E51 measured it on two models: 1.76x the tier's 16K prefill on
Swift (drive-bound), but slower than the memory map when the model sits in the page cache (Gemma pp4k
260 against 573 tok/s), so it ships opt-in. The new switch --moe-prefill-source (env LLAMA_ARG_MOE_PREFILL_SOURCE,
llama_context_params.moe_prefill_source, 0 = mmap, 1 = p3) chooses it:

  mmap (default): llama_moe_cache::has_miss_source returns false, so sched_copy_experts runs upstream's uploads from the
  host tensor, the same calls with the same offsets and sizes as before 0008, whatever the miss source. The slot path
  (decode, and the misses of small ubatches) still uses the ring or tier as in P3.
  p3: 0008's behaviour, unchanged.

p3 with --moe-miss-source mmap is refused: the context is not created and the error says p3 needs a ring or tier miss
source (an invalid value is refused the same way). If the miss source is asked for but cannot be set up, its existing
warning now adds "(nor --moe-prefill-source p3)". The P3 load line, which reports the miss source, now ends with
"prefill source p3: large-batch copies from the source too (0008: ...)" or "prefill source mmap: large-batch copies from
the host tensors (upstream)". llama_moe_source_params gains a prefill field (last member), used only for that line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
